                "Showing severe hypoxaemia and hypercapnia. 3076 Immediate resuscitation is critical in managing respiratory arrest.",
                "The focus is on opening the airway, restoring effective breathing, and preventing cardiac arrest.",
                "Ensure a patent airway by positioning the head (tilt and chin lift or jaw thrust in cases of trauma).",
                "Clear the airway of any obstructions (e.g., foreign body, secretions).",
                "If the child is not breathing, provide rescue breaths with a bag -valve mask (BVM) or mouth -to- mouth if BVM is not available.",
                "Deliver one breath every 2 -3 seconds (20-30 breaths per minute).",
                "Chest compressions (if no pulse or signs of life).",
                "Start cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) if the child remains unresponsive and pulse is not palpable or <60 beats per minute with poor perfusion.",
                "Compression -to-ventilation ratio: 15:2 for two -rescuer CPR, and 30:2 for one -rescuer CPR."
