                    "Atopic dermatitis is a common, chronic skin condition affecting both children and adults.",
                    "Management involves regular use of emollients, topical anti -inflammatory therapies, and addressing exacerbating factors.",
                    "While many patients outgrow the condition, others may experience persistent symptoms into adulthood.",
                    "Recognizing complications, such as secondary infections, and escalating treatment when necessary, including the use of phototherapy or biologic agents, is essential for optimal patient care.",
                    "Irritant contact dermatitis (ICD) is a form of dermatitis caused by direct chemical or physical damage to the skin following exposure to an irritant.",
                    "It is the most common form of contact dermatitis and results from the non-immunologic response of the skin to irritants such as soaps, detergents, acids, or friction.",
                    "Unlike allergic contact dermatitis, ICD does not involve an allergic reaction and can occur in anyone, given sufficient exposure to the irritant. \u2022 Erythema (Redness).",
