                "A skin biopsy may be required to identify the underlying condition responsible for erythroderma.",
                "Regular application of emollients helps maintain skin hydration and restore the skin barrier. o Oral corticosteroids (e.g., prednisolone ) may be necessary for patients with severe inflammation, particularly in cases where drug reactions or autoimmune diseases are the cause. o Psoriasis.",
                "Treat with systemic agents such as methotrexate, cyclosporin, or biologic agents (e.g., TNF-alpha inhibitors ). o Cutaneous T -cell lymphoma.",
                "Manage with systemic chemotherapy or radiotherapy. o Drug-induced erythroderma.",
                "Immediate discontinuation of the offending drug is crucial. \u2022 Long-term corticosteroid use.",
                "Should be avoided if possible due to the risk of side effects, including immunosuppression, hyperglycaemia, and osteoporosis. o Ciclosporin.",
