                "Typically affects two or more sites (e.g., oral, ocular, genital). \u2022 A history of medication use, especially those known to trigger TEN (e.g., sulfonamides, anticonvulsants, NSAIDs, allopurinol ).",
                "Typically 2 g/kg over 3-5 days. o IVIG is believed to inhibit Fas-mediated keratinocyte apoptosis, thus reducing further skin necrosis. o The use of systemic corticosteroids in TEN remains controversial, as they may increase the risk of infection."
