                "It results from 471 autoantibodies targeting hemidesmosomes in the basement membrane of the epidermis, specifically against BP180 and BP230 proteins.",
                "This leads to a subepidermal blistering process, distinguishing it from pemphigus vulgaris (which has intraepidermal blistering).",
                "This is the gold standard for diagnosis.",
                "It shows a linear pattern of IgG and C3 deposition at the dermoepidermal junction, confirming the autoimmune nature of bullous pemphigoid. \u2022 Serum antibodies (ELISA).",
                "Detection of circulating anti-BP180 and anti-BP230 antibodies helps confirm the diagnosis and can also be used to monitor disease activity."
