                "Removal of one thyroid lobe, may be sufficient for small, low -risk papillary carcinomas. o Total thyroidectomy.",
                "Recommended for larger nodules, malignant nodules, or when there is suspicion of metastatic disease. \u2022 Radioactive iodine (I -131) is commonly used to treat autonomously functioning nodules or toxic multinodular goitres, as it selectively destroys hyperfunctioning thyroid tissue. \u2022 Surgery.",
                "May be indicated for large toxic nodules or multinodular goitres causing compressive symptoms. \u2022 Antithyroid drugs.",
