        "synonyms": [],
        "recognition": {
            "typical": [
                "Include central obesity, moon face, hypertension, proximal muscle weakness, skin changes, and osteoporosis. \u2022 First-line investigations include the 24-hour urinary cortisol, low-dose dexamethasone suppression test, and ACTH levels.",
                "Conn\u2019s syndrome, also known as primary hyperaldosteronism, is an endocrine disorder characterised by the excessive production of aldosterone from the adrenal glands, leading to hypertension and hypokalaemia.",
                "The condition is usually caused by either an aldosterone - producing adrenal adenoma (Conn\u2019s adenom \u2022 Hypertension.",
                "Low potassium levels, which may present with: o Muscle weakness or cramps. o Fatigue. o Numbness or tingling (paraesthesia). o Palpitations or arrhythmias. o Polyuria (increased urination) and polydipsia (increased thirst), due to potassium depletion. \u2022 Headaches. \u2022 Nocturia.",
                "Due to electrolyte disturbances. \u2022 Metabolic alkalosis.",
                "Increased bicarbonate levels in the blood secondary to potassium loss."
            ],
            "atypical": [],
            "examination": [
                "Are inconclusive. \u2022 ACTH levels are measured from the veins draining the pituitary gland (petrosal sinuses).",
                "If the ACTH levels are significantly higher here than in the peripheral veins, this confirms pituitary ACTH secretion. \u2022 Low-dose dexamethasone suppression test.",
                "Cushing\u2019s disease is confirmed if cortisol is not suppressed after low-dose dexamethasone, indicating loss of feedback inhibition. \u2022 Plasma ACTH.",
                "Elevated ACTH indicates an ACTH-dependent cause, pointing towards either Cushing\u2019s disease or ectopic ACTH production. \u2022 High-dose dexamethasone test.",
                "Helps differentiate Cushing\u2019s disease (partial suppression of cortisol) from ectopic ACTH production (no suppression). \u2022 MRI pituitary.",
                "Identifies pituitary adenomas, though smaller ones may be missed.",
                "Inhibits cortisol synthesis by blocking the enzyme 11 \u03b2- hydroxylase. o Ketoconazole.",
                "An antifungal that also inhibits cortisol synthesis. o Pasireotide.",
                "A somatostatin analogue that directly inhibits ACTH release from the pituitary. o Mitotane.",
                "A potent adrenolytic agent used in refractory cases."
            ],
            "redFlags": []
        },
