                "According to NICE guidelines, the diagnosis can often be made clinically, especially if the patient has the classic symptoms, supported by blood tests.",
                "Encourage bed rest and increased fluid intake to help manage fatigue and systemic symptoms.",
                "Most patients recover fully with rest, though fatigue may persist for weeks.",
                "Use paracetamol or ibuprofen to relieve sore throat, headache, and fever.",
                "Provides symptomatic relief of fever, sore throat, and generalised discomfort.",
                "Patients should avoid contact sports or strenuous activity for at least 4 -6 weeks, especially if splenomegaly is present, to reduce the risk of splenic rupture."
