                "Lipase is more specific for pancreatitis than amylase.",
                "Raised bilirubin, ALP, or ALT may suggest gallstone pancreatitis.",
                "Raised white cell count is common, indicating an inflammatory response.",
                "Used to monitor kidney function and detect dehydration.",
                "Elevated CRP levels are a marker of inflammation and may correlate with the severity of the pancreatitis.",
                "Hypocalcaemia can occur in severe cases.",
                "Often used first to detect gallstones and assess the biliary tree for obstruction, which may have caused the pancreatitis."
