                "Distant metastases, commonly to the liver, peritoneum, or lungs.",
                "Whipple procedure (pancreaticoduodenectomy).",
                "The most common surgery for tumours located in the head of the pancreas.",
                "Involves the removal of the head of the pancreas, the duodenum, part of the stomach, the gallbladder, and bile duct, followed by reattachment of the digestive tract.",
                "Surgery is only possible in early-stage pancreatic cancer (approximately 20% of cases) where the tumour has not invaded major blood vessels or metastasised. 1922 Distal pancreatectomy.",
                "For tumours in the body or tail of the pancreas.",
                "Removes the affected portion of the pancreas and sometimes the spleen.",
                "Used to shrink tumours before surgery in patients with borderline resectable tumours.",
                "FOLFIRINOX (combination of 5-fluorouracil, oxaliplatin, irinotecan, and leucovorin ) or gemcitabine -based regimens."
