                "CA 19-9 is not specific to pancreatic cancer but can help monitor treatment response and detect recurrence.",
                "Ultrasound is readily available and non -invasive, but it may miss small pancreatic tumours or those in the body and tail of the pancreas.",
                "CT scan is the gold standard for diagnosing pancreatic cancer and assessing the extent of the disease.",
                "A pancreatic protocol CT provides detailed images of the pancreas, surrounding tissues, and vessels, crucial for staging and determining resectability.",
