                "Cervical cancer develops slowly over time, often preceded by a precancerous stage known as cervical intraepithelial neoplasia (CIN), which can progress to invasive cancer if left untreated.",
                "Cervical cancer is classified into two main types.",
                "Arises from the squamous cells lining the outer part of the cervix, accounting for about 70 -80% of cases.",
                "Originates from the glandular cells of the endocervix, responsible for 10 - 20% of cases but often more difficult to detect."
