                "Treatment for cervical cancer depends on the stage of the disease, the patient\u2019s general health, and whether the cancer is localised or has spread.",
                "The main treatment modalities include surgery, radiotherapy, and chemotherapy.",
                "Radical hysterectomy with removal of the cervix, uterus, part of the vagina, and surrounding tissues.",
                "Removes the tumour and any affected tissues, providing definitive treatment for early-stage disease.",
                "Standard treatment for stage IA2 to IIA cervical cancer, particularly in younger women who wish to preserve ovarian function.",
                "Conization or Loop Electrosurgical Excision Procedure (LEEP).",
                "Used for very early -stage cancer ( stage IA1 ) or precancerous lesions (CIN) to remove abnormal cervical tissue while preserving fertility.",
