                "In cases of leptomeningeal spread, malignant cells in the CSF confirm the diagnosis.",
                "Treatment for brain metastases depends on factors such as the number of metastases, the location within the brain, the primary cancer type, the patient\u2019s overall health, and the presence of systemic disease.",
                "Goals of treatment include controlling brain metastases, alleviating symptoms, and improving quality of life.",
                "Dosage: 8\u201316 mg/day, tapering down over time.",
                "Reduces cerebral oedema and alleviates symptoms such as headache and neurological deficits.",
                "Used to relieve symptoms caused by increased intracranial pressure from oedema around the metastases.",
