                "While chronic alcoholism is the most common cause, other factors such as malnutrition, prolonged vomiting, or bariatric surger y can also lead to thiamine deficiency.",
                "Wernicke\u2019s encephalopathy is part of a spectrum of alcohol-related brain injury and can progress to Korsakoff\u2019s syndrome, a chronic condition characterised by severe memory deficits, if untreated.",
                "The classic triad of symptoms in Wernicke\u2019s encephalopathy is.",
                "Weakness or paralysis of the eye muscles, causing double vision or difficulty moving the eyes.",
                "Difficulty with balance and coordination, leading to unsteady walking."
