                "A CT scan provides detailed imaging of the kidneys and can help distinguish between benign cysts and solid tumours.",
                "It also assesses the size, location, and extent of the tumour, as well as any local invasion or metastases.",
                "Ultrasound can detect simple cysts but may miss small or complex tumours, which require further imaging.",
                "MRI is useful in patients where CT contrast is contraindicated, such as in cases of renal impairment.",
                "MRI provides detailed images of soft tissue, renal vasculature, and tumour involvement in surrounding tissues.",
                "Microscopic haematuria is a common finding.",
                "Urinalysis can detect blood or other abnormalities, but is not diagnostic for renal cancer on its own. e) Full Blood Count (FBC) and Serum Biochemistry."
