                "In optic neuritis, the affected eye has a delayed or reduced pupillary reaction to light.",
                "Fundoscopy (direct or indirect ophthalmoscopy).",
                "In retrobulbar optic neuritis (most common), the optic disc may appear normal initially, as inflammation occurs behind the eye.",
                "In papillitis (inflammation of the optic disc), the optic disc may appear swollen and hyperaemic.",
                "Fundoscopy helps differentiate between anterior and retrobulbar optic neuritis.",
                "MRI is used to detect inflammation of the optic nerve and identify white matter lesions in the brain, which are indicative of multiple sclerosis (MS).",
