                "If some of the retina is visible, signs of a retinal tear, neovascularisation, or detachment may be noted.",
                "Ophthalmoscopy helps assess the extent of the haemorrhage and detect any associated retinal pathology.",
                "Can show blood in the vitreous cavity and detect associated complications like retinal detachment or posterior vitreous detachment.",
                "B-scan is crucial when the haemorrhage is too dense to visualise the retina, helping to rule out retinal detachment or other structural issues.",
                "Useful to assess retinal neovascularisation or ischemic areas in cases of diabetic retinopathy or other vascular conditions.",
                "Helps to identify the source of bleeding and assess the retinal blood vessels for new abnormal vessels. 2109 Findings.",
