                "Diagnosis is supported by lung function tests and a thorough clinical history.",
                "Spirometry with Bronchodilator Reversibility Testing.",
                "Spirometry measures lung function by assessing forced expiratory volume in 1 second (FEV1) and forced vital capacity (FVC).",
                "In ACO, spirometry may show persistent airflow limitation (FEV1/FVC <70%) with partial reversibility after bronchodilator use (improvement in FEV1 \u226512% but incomplete normalisation).",
                "Monitoring diurnal variation in PEF can reveal variability, characteristic of asthma, with periods of improvement and worsening, especially with bronchodilators.",
                "Fractional Exhaled Nitric Oxide (FeNO) Test.",
