                "Persistent respiratory symptoms (cough, dyspnoea, hemoptysis), weight loss, and risk factors such as smoking.",
                "May show a mass, nodule, or pleural effusion.",
                "Detailed assessment of tumour location and spread.",
                "Histological confirmation: 2268 Tissue biopsy showing malignant cells (adenocarcinoma, squamous cell carcinoma, small cell carcinoma, etc.).",
                "Based on the TNM classification (Tumour size, Node involvement, Metastasis), determined by imaging and biopsy.",
                "Treatment of primary lung cancer depends on the type (NSCLC or SCLC), stage, and the patient\u2019s overall health.",
                "Multidisciplinary care involving oncologists, surgeons, and radiologists is essential.",
                "Lobectomy or pneumonectomy is the preferred option in stages I and II if the tumour is resectable and the patient has adequate lung function.",
