                "Many patients, particularly those with Stage 1 pulmonary sarcoidosis, do not require treatment, as the disease may resolve spontaneously.",
                "Symptomatic or progressive disease: 2287 Oral corticosteroids (Prednisolone).",
                "Initial dose: 20-40 mg daily for 6 -12 weeks, followed by a gradual taper over 6 -12 months.",
                "Corticosteroids suppress inflammation and granuloma formation.",
                "Symptomatic pulmonary disease, significant extrapulmonary involvement (e.g., cardiac, ocular, neurological), or hypercalcaemia.",
