                "A score of 10 or more points is required for diagnosis, provided the patient has a positive ANA as an entry criterion.",
                "Thrombocytopenia (4 points), leukopenia (3 points), haemolytic anaemia (4 points).",
                "Seizure (5 points), psychosis (3 points).",
                "Malar rash (6 points), discoid rash (4 points), photosensitivity (2 points), oral ulcers (2 points).",
                "Proteinuria (10 points), renal biopsy consistent with lupus nephritis (8 -10 points).",
                "Photosensitivity is common in SLE, so patients should use broad-spectrum sunscreen and wear protective clothing to reduce skin flares. 2390 Regular exercise.",
                "Low-impact activities (e.g., walking, swimming) help improve fatigue, maintain joint mobility, and reduce the risk of cardiovascular disease."
