                "Symptoms include deformity, pain, and inability to move the limb.",
                "Loss of consciousness, confusion, or neurological deficits following head trauma suggest traumatic brain injury (TBI), including concussions, contusions, or intracranial hemorrhage.",
                "Symptoms such as shortness of breath, chest pain, or flail chest indicate rib fractures, pneumothorax, or hemothorax.",
                "Abdominal pain, tenderness, or distension may indicate solid organ injuries (e.g., liver, spleen) or hollow viscus perforation.",
                "Back pain, numbness, weakness, or loss of bladder/bowel control may indicate spinal cord injury or vertebral fractures. 2576 Shock."
