                "Continuous monitoring of oxygenation, ventilation, and vital signs is essential, with frequent assessments of ABGs and clinical response. 3078 Respiratory distress syndrome (RDS), also known as hyaline membrane disease, is a condition primarily seen in preterm infants due to insufficient surfactant production in the lungs.",
                "Surfactant is a substance that lowers surface tension in the alveoli, preventing them from collapsing at the end of expiration.",
                "Without enough surfactant, the lungs struggle to inflate, leading to atelectasis (collapse of lung tissue), poor gas exchange, and hypoxia.",
                "RDS is most common in infants born before 34 weeks of gestatio n, with the incidence increasing the earlier the infant is born.",
                "Rapid breathing, often >60 breaths per minute.",
                "A compensatory mechanism used to maintain positive airway pressure and keep the alveoli open.",
                "Widening of the nostrils with each breath as a sign of increased work of breathing."
